{
 "_comment": [
  "The persisted-format surface that scripts/check_storage_format.py computes, and the record of the approval that admitted it (FMT-1, docs/design-rules.md#fmt-1).",
  "Persisted formats are frozen until Scarab leaves pre-release. This file changes only in a storage format change of its own, approved by the owner in the chat session doing the work in answer to an explicit question asked there before the change was written.",
  "`approval` records that question and the owner's decision, in neutral words and never as a quotation, with their UTC times and the digest of the surface they admit. It is evidence of the approval, never an approval itself. `approval` is null only for the baseline: the surface of main (bc0e4995a, after #994 merged) on 2026-11-14, when the freeze began, which approves nothing."
 ],
 "approval": {
  "question": "Storage format change for PlutusV4 reference scripts (#85 item 2), restated in the freeze guard's terms: may I record this storage format change as approved in docs/data/storage-format.json, in a (storage)! PR of its own that item (2) stacks on? (1) The stored script kind gains PlutusV4; enums are written as an ordinal byte, so kinds 0-3 keep their bytes and RocksDB/utxo.bin values written before stay readable (no UtxoKeyLayout change). (2) V10's sidecar schema is frozen with the four-kind ScriptKind, as FrozenEra was for V9, so the V7-V10 fingerprints don't move. (3) A new snapshot version V11 (magic SCRBSNPB) with a value-preserving V10 to V11 migration, fixtures/snapshot-v11 converted from v10, and a suite reading the committed V10 files; deployed stores migrate on open. (4) ScriptKind lives in ledger/Scripts.scala, outside the guard's allowed paths, so the PR also touches it and the ledger/storage/tools files with ScriptKind matches, each refusing PlutusV4 where Conway does, so 11.1 behaviour is unchanged, with refusal tests. Followed in the session by the alternative, if Leios and the 11.x networks can write one format: modify V10 in place instead, with no V11.",
  "asked_at": "2026-11-16T17:38:40Z",
  "decision": "Approved: V10 is modified in place, with no V11, because Leios and the 11.x networks can write one format and no deployment runs V10. The stored script kind gains PlutusV4, kinds 0 to 3 keeping their bytes; V10's sidecar fingerprint moves and its fixtures are regenerated; the frozen schemas of V5 to V9 keep their fingerprints through a frozen four-kind script kind; the ledger files whose exhaustive matches follow the kind name PlutusV4, refused wherever an era before Dijkstra refuses it, and the guard's list of paths a storage format change may touch gains them; in a pull request of its own.",
  "decided_at": "2026-11-16T17:40:45Z",
  "surface_sha256": "715c8034d7f3de9c9c24320691796f94009d4eb720bcf1d20ee42daba529985f"
 },
